"""Rich good-state ticker lines.

A healthy member no longer gets a bare "X is healthy." Every row here says what they are doing, with whom, and ties it to the clan's story: another
living member ({B}, and {C} when three or more are alive), the member the clan lost most recently ({D}, only when someone has died), the day number
({day}), the faction's place ({place}), the last raid / patrol / match, the supplies. Rows are (scope, English template, Polish template) side by side
(the same registry pattern as clan_story_solo.ROWS); scope "*" = both factions, "W" Wolves only, "S" Seraphites only.
Placeholders: {A} the member the line is about, {B} another living member, {C} a third, {D} the latest dead member, {day} {week} {place}
{place_gen}/{place_at}/{place_to}/{place_from}/{place_ins} (Polish cases), {enemies}. Polish: {A?ł|ła} gender switch, {AB?li|ły} plural (feminine only
when everyone is female), names never declined.
Rendered length must stay <= clan_story.WIDGET_MAX (118); tools/tests/test_clan_story_rich.py checks it for every row and every name.
"""


def R(scope, en, pl):
    return (scope, en, pl)


